# TastyGo — DevOps Deployment Project

A hands-on DevOps project demonstrating application containerization, CI pipeline automation, container image publishing, and AWS infrastructure provisioning using Terraform.

TastyGo is a food delivery frontend that I containerized using Docker, integrated with Jenkins, and deployed on two AWS EC2 instances using an image published to GitHub Container Registry (GHCR).

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates how application code moves from GitHub through a Jenkins pipeline, becomes a Docker image, and is published to GHCR for deployment on AWS EC2 instances.

The AWS infrastructure is provisioned using Terraform, while Docker is installed automatically on both instances using EC2 user data.

**Deployment approach:** Jenkins automates image building and publishing. Pulling the image and running the container on EC2 are manual steps in the current implementation.

